371ad09de9" :question/math-academy-id "q-139995" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$, equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\n Find $⟨x(t),y(t)⟩$, if\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2}-2t-3,\\,y(t)={t}^{2}-1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3) \\\\  & =-4\\cdot 0+(-3)\\cdot 3+0\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =0-9+0 \\\\  & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-139995/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "efed2bff-625e-556d-99a3-9b51f9d68937"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-139995"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-43815/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "3952e819-bab6-5a3b-b2f1-43a4ad1b3e3b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43815/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "5f7cf48d-5feb-5df8-8f83-c51822ca2c2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43815/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "31db2f69-3114-508b-bcbb-dedfa7845096" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43815/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "c4a663cf-800b-5e1a-b5a6-d940494d7dde" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43815/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "0e7df757-a1f9-57da-a070-9b68a4becab6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43815/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c18613b-422b-54da-80f2-3258e4f932db" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-43815/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-43815/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-43815/selection/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" "q-43815/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-43815/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" "q-43815/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-43815" :question/id #uuid "69eed8f6-c7de-5ae2-bbb9-21c428d14ef6" :question/math-academy-id "q-43815" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$, equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(-2)y(-2).\n$$\n\n Find $⟨x(t),y(t)⟩$, if\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2}-5,\\,y(t)={t}^{2}-3t.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(-2)y(-2) \\\\  & =(-4)\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot (-2)+(-1)\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =8+2-10 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-43815/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "efed2bff-625e-556d-99a3-9b51f9d68937"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-43815"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42250"] :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$, equipped with the inner product\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(-1)y(-1)+x(0)y(0)+x(1)y(1).\n$$\n\n Find $⟨x(t),y(t)⟩$, if\n\n$$\nx(t)=5-2t+{t}^{2},\\,y(t)=t-1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =x(-1)y(-1)+x(0)y(0)+x(1)y(1) \\\\  & =8\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot (-1)+4\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =-16-5+0 \\\\  & =-21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-139996/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "725c3a11-a2e0-5f15-bd74-c1390cccc290" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139996/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "1da3cb8e-daf9-55fa-a19c-601163be104e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139996/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "89da18cf-0577-5466-b658-07d7ba369211" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139996/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "37903fd9-afaf-5791-9bee-7fbc177ccae1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139996/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "37ff5c2d-e7b1-5bb1-82b8-52911db01de7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139996/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5bcae02d-71e8-551c-a2c9-bc0369de5ad1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-139996/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-139996/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-139996/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-139996/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-139996/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-139996/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-139996" :question/id #uuid "e4b5e657-b208-5234-bf29-13d5bc2c6c08" :question/math-academy-id "q-139996" :question/problem "Let $V={R}_{2}[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$, equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩=x(-2)y(-2)+x(-1)y(-1)+x(0)y(0).\n$$\n\n Find $⟨x(t),y(t)⟩$, if\n\n$$\nx(t)={t}^{2}+3t+2,\\,y(t)=t-1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =x(-2)y(-2)+x(-1)y(-1)+x(0)y(0). \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-3)+0\\cdot (-2)+2\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =0+0-2 \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-139996/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "efed2bff-625e-556d-99a3-9b51f9d68937"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-139996"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42254"] :question/problem "Let $V=C[-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$ Find $⟨{sin}^{2}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n⟨{sin}^{2}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,$ $\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{\\pi /2}{sin}^{2}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3}|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =[\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3}]-[\\frac{1}{3}(-1)^{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-139997/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b9f17853-f9e4-590c-be97-60602c224ce8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139997/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "b126e052-2cea-5df6-960e-8edbb2a68f89" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139997/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" :answer/id #uuid "68171de2-88d3-505f-a12e-dacc0e7b9d7b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139997/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "da300585-c499-58ee-8d8a-dc05ef4fe4b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139997/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "8356cbfc-eadd-57ca-81c7-a3d4eb37409c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-139997/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "cbdcab7d-3226-56df-b9bf-d5cbbe4e6107" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-139997/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer-field/choices ["q-139997/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-139997/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-139997/selection/e9bc05c525076ace5dedc0dc52c4f8497f441cd3bf97b666736f75acd9994b26" "q-139997/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-139997/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-139997" :question/id #uuid "459ccc68-d7d9-5cf4-b185-3c6efbba8e15" :question/math-academy-id "q-139997" :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,\\pi ],$ the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,\\pi ].$ Find $⟨t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n⟨t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nLet's use integration by parts. We denote\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t & ⟹ & {u}^{′}=1, \\\\ {v}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & ⟹ & v=\\int {v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for the integration by parts, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =uv{|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t){|}_{0}^{\\pi }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(\\pi \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi +0\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡0)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t{|}_{0}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =0+(\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-139997/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c553cb8-9f5c-5fa5-bc43-db7d7b64755f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-139997"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-42256"] :question/problem "Let $V=C[0,2],$ the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[0,2].$ Find $⟨t,{e}^{t}⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n⟨t,{e}^{t}⟩={\\int }_{0}^{2}t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nLet's use integration by parts. We denote\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=t & ⟹ & {u}^{′}=1, \\\\ {v}^{′}={e}^{t} & ⟹ & v=\\int {v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t=\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t={e}^{t}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting into the formula for the integration by parts, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}t{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t & =uv{|}_{0}^{2}-{\\int }_{0}^{2}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(t{e}^{t}){|}_{0}^{2}-{\\int }_{0}^{2}{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(2{e}^{2}-0{e}^{0})-{e}^{t}{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =2{e}^{2}-({e}^{2}-1) \\\\  & ={e}^{2}+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-42255/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "cc7266f3-dbbe-58a8-b5b3-3adbd50fff03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42255/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "faaf0265-6393-53f6-9e40-c4626a51666a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42255/selection/8edf36f0d0c04b8e0e3f881a66fab0f1901a06368d5ca1f6d437f77714de6bc5" :answer/id #uuid "373c8e9c-cd43-5cd4-9102-44bf90a376d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{\\pi }{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42255/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" :answer/id #uuid "f4c97068-908a-5d68-a03d-6a6c3bc570d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42255/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer/id #uuid "732b6fe3-f810-581e-95f6-7e6d1fd4a414" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-42255/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "06a3c639-92d1-557f-8db2-57d3ced9275b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-42255/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer-field/choices ["q-42255/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-42255/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-42255/selection/8edf36f0d0c04b8e0e3f881a66fab0f1901a06368d5ca1f6d437f77714de6bc5" "q-42255/selection/3a619fab2616dab0463f9c76cb72cd9f101e45e62111356a5b0b111e062a8dcf" "q-42255/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-42255" :question/id #uuid "3cc9ef9c-fc7a-5c00-b52f-1c2bdfbdac79" :question/math-academy-id "q-42255" :question/problem "Let $V=C[-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0],$ the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[-\\frac{\\pi }{2},0].$ Find $⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,{cos}^{2}⁡t⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,{cos}^{2}⁡t⟩={\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the substitution $u=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ $\\text{d}u=-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi /2}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t{cos}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =-{\\int }_{0}^{1}{u}^{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{{u}^{3}}{3}{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{(1)^{3}}{3}]-[-\\frac{(0)^{3}}{3}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}+0 \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-42255/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c553cb8-9f5c-5fa5-bc43-db7d7b64755f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-42255"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-43855/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer/id #uuid "981d2a8a-95e3-5739-b087-202d0ce9df76" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43855/selection/8005c65f2a515e841c435400ecdcba0e95ad7c08625aaa531721c2396d0f7dbf" :answer/id #uuid "c6c1139d-f7ca-5f55-9439-ef5b8b46746d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43855/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" :answer/id #uuid "4f0608d1-1377-5e74-b20a-1d527a336991" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43855/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "c4e3ee02-f048-5633-ae7b-1b136526bc54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43855/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff" :answer/id #uuid "fcee6a49-1328-5ab1-8e00-550ceca991fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-43855/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4c6e170a-4c93-5b96-a7a8-d2fa5353391c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-43855/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" :answer-field/choices ["q-43855/selection/5ab3573096b30d3c5d3c378e667364cbb062f921e9b1002441e594f0774a669d" "q-43855/selection/8005c65f2a515e841c435400ecdcba0e95ad7c08625aaa531721c2396d0f7dbf" "q-43855/selection/4e2cb386499e1926f074a7bcd422a63175a237204a3823f0fa6c86b56d301873" "q-43855/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-43855/selection/b13ac151352392d38026eed875b911708c50c896d6c09463410ac041030163ff"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-43855" :question/id #uuid "94de83fd-a553-50b8-b88f-58c41cefa36b" :question/math-academy-id "q-43855" :question/problem "Let $V=C[-1,0],$ the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $[-1,0].$ Find $⟨t,\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}⟩$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$$\n⟨x(t),y(t)⟩={\\int }_{-1}^{0}x(t)y(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n⟨t,\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}⟩={\\int }_{-1}^{0}t\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the substitution $u=1-{t}^{2},$ $\\text{d}u=-2t\\,\\text{d}t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{0}t\\sqrt{1-{t}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}t & =-\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\sqrt{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}{u}^{3/2}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}{u}^{3/2}\\,{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =[-\\frac{1}{3}(1)^{3/2}]-[-\\frac{1}{3}(0)^{3/2}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-43855/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c553cb8-9f5c-5fa5-bc43-db7d7b64755f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-43855"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5542"] :question/problem "An inner product on $V = \\mathbb{R}^3$ is given by $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle =  3 x_1 y_1 + x_2 y_2 + 7 x_3 y_3.$ Find $\\langle \\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y} \\rangle,$ if\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14054904/assets/028bb3befd54071fcae6cb88bd3e054d3325557ef31274ec23146e1da81f8258.png)" :question/worked-solution "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x,y⟩ & =3{x}_{1}{y}_{1}+{x}_{2}{y}_{2}+7{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-3)+(-2)\\cdot 1+7\\cdot 0\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-9-2+0 \\\\  & =-11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5543"] :question/problem "Let $V=\\mathbb{R}_2[t]$ be the vector space of all polynomials of degree at most $2$, equipped with the inner product \n\n$$\n\\langle {x}(t), {y}(t) \\rangle = x(1)y(1) + x(2)y(2) + x(3)y(3).\n$$\n\n Find $\\langle \\mathbf{x}(t), \\mathbf{y}(t) \\rangle,$ if\n\n$$\n{x}(t) = 1-2t+3t^2,\n\t\\quad\n\t{y}(t) = t-t^2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Computing the inner product according to the definition, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨x(t),y(t)⟩ & =x(1)y(1)+x(2)y(2)+x(3)y(3) \\\\  & =2\\cdot 0+9\\cdot (-2)+22\\cdot (-6) \\\\  & =0-18-132 \\\\  & =-150.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5544"] :question/problem "Let $V=\\mathcal{C}\\left[0,2\\pi\\right],$ the vector space of all functions that are continuous on $\\left[0,2\\pi\\right].$ Find $\\langle \\sin t, \\cos t \\rangle$ if the inner product on $V$ is defined as\n\n$$\n\\langle x(t),y(t) \\rangle = \\displaystyle\\int_{0}^{2\\pi} x(t) y(t) \\, \\textrm{d}t.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to evaluate\n\n$$\n\\langle \\sin t, \\cos t \\rangle  =  \\int_{0}^{2\\pi}\\sin{t} \\cos{t} \\,\\textrm{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can evaluate this integral using the identity $\\sin2t =2\\sin t\\cos t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t{|}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4\\pi -\\operatorname{cos}⁡0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(1-1) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
